{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Why is it that, etc.</b> As if to say: why did you abandon this man who bestowed kindness upon you? Or it may mean that he takes exception to the time during which they left him standing from then until they returned to call him, his reason being that it is not proper conduct that a stranger should do a kindness with them and they should come and leave him standing outside. Or it may mean further that even though Yitro objected to their socializing with men, he said that this one would differ from all of them — and that is his saying <b>why is it that</b>, etc., for his deeds prove that he is a man of kindness — all the more so according to their words (Shemot Rabbah 1:32) that they told him the waters rose to meet him: behold, this one is extraordinary with the most extraordinary praises."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:36.862907475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}